WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.342
A recursive common table expression is used when one result leads to the next result repeatedly.

00:00:06.342 --> 00:00:08.602
It has two main parts.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:11.917
The anchor term creates the starting rows.

00:00:11.917 --> 00:00:16.728
The recursive term uses the rows already found to locate the next level.

00:00:17.391 --> 00:00:19.898
A company hierarchy is a good example.

00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:21.798
We can start with the president.

00:00:21.798 --> 00:00:25.108
Then we find employees who report to the president.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:29.348
After that, we find employees who report to those employees.

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:33.833
The process continues until no more matching employees are found.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.933
Do not think of recursion as mysterious.

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:41.458
Think of it as start here, find the next level, and repeat.
